<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30700" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nĕmausum</span></b> , i,
		n., and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nĕmausus</span></b> , i, f., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a city in Gallia
				Narbonensis, noted for its springs</i>, now <i>Nismes</i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b> Form
			Nemausum, <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 4, 5, §
			37</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			Form Nemausus, <i><span class="en">Mel. 2, 5, 2</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Aus. Clar. Urb. 14, 33</span></i>; cf.
					<i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell. 3751</span></i>;
			<i><span class="en">2157</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nĕmausensis</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nĕmausiensis</span></b> , e, <i>adj., of</i> or <i>belonging to
				Nemausis</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">caseus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					11, 42, 97, § 240</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ager,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 9,
					8, 9, § 29</span></i>
			. —<i>Plur.</i> as <i>subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nĕmausenses</span></b> , ium,
			m., <i>the inhabitants of Nemausus</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Plin.
				3, 4, 5, § 37</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Suet.
				Tib. 13</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell.
		198</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
